# Nova - environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root (or Config/.env). Values already set in your real
# environment win: `load_env()` never overwrites a key that already exists.
# Nothing here is required - `nova doctor` reports which engines are usable, and
# scripts/local_setup.ps1 gets a fully local stack running with no key at all.

# --- cloud engines (each one is optional; llama and ollama are local at 1-2, these are 3-6) ---

# Gemini - https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Google AI Studio accepts either name; Nova checks both.
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Groq - https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# OpenAI - https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face Inference Providers - https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
# Create a FINE-GRAINED token and tick "Make calls to Inference Providers", or every call
# comes back 401/403. Free accounts carry no included credit (PRO adds $2/month), so Nova
# reports a 402 as "no Inference Providers credit" and points at `nova engine use ollama`.
HF_TOKEN=
# Policy suffix on the model id picks the provider: :fastest, :cheapest, :preferred,
# or an exact provider name. `nova engine models hf` lists what the router serves.
# HF_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct:fastest
# HF_MAX_TOKENS=700

# --- local inference (no key, this is the default path) ---

# llama.cpp serving a GGUF downloaded from Hugging Face (priority 1). Start the server with:
#   llama-server -hf unsloth/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-GGUF:Q4_K_M --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
# Nova adopts whatever model id that server is hosting, so LLAMA_CPP_MODEL stays unset unless
# the server hosts several. llama.cpp listens on 9931 by default - pass --port to match this URL.
# LLAMA_CPP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# LLAMA_CPP_MAX_TOKENS=700

# OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# --- paths ---

# Where .nova/ (settings, memory, traces) and workspace/ live. Defaults to the repo root.
# NOVA_HOME=C:\path\to\Nova-System-AI
# The sandbox the file and shell tools are confined to.
# NOVA_WORKSPACE=C:\path\to\Nova-System-AI\workspace

# --- permission gate ---

# NOVA_YOLO=1 grants write/exec/destructive actions without prompting (hard blocks
# still fire). Leave this commented out unless you are automating inside a throwaway
# VM - it applies to every run that reads this file, not just one command.
# NOVA_YOLO=1
